titre$ Key to the teleomorphs of the Europeau species of Botryobasidium
1,2 $ Clamps present, at least on particular hyphae in the bas idiome
1,7 $ Clamps completely absent
2,3 $ Cystidia present.
2,4 $ Cystidia absent
3,0 $ Hyphae and cystidia encrusted, spores (4.5-)5-6 x 2.5-3 µm  $ B. pilosellum
3,0 $ Hyphae and cystidia without encrustation, spores (6---)7-8.5 x (3-)3.5-4.5 $ B. sassofratinoense
4,0 $ Spores broadly navicular, 9-12 x 5-6(-6.5) µm . Anamorph: Haplotrichum medium $ B. medium*
4,5 $ Spores narrower, up to 3(-3.5) µm  wide
5,0 $ Clamps often absent on basal hyphae, spores navicular to subcylindrical, 6---10 x 1.5-3 µm  $ B. intertextum
5,6 $ Clamps present at all septa, spores otherwise
6,0 $ Basidia large, (10-)20-25(-30) x 7-9µm , spores navicular, 6.5-8 x 2.5-3(-3.5) µm . Anamorph unknown $ B. subcoronatum
6,0 $ Basidia smaller, 7.5-10(-12) x 4--5 µm , spores navicular, 6-7.5(-8) x 2.5-3 µm . Anamorph of the Haplotrichum type $ B. ponderosum
7,8 $ Basidia with 4-sterigmata, spores ornamented with evident aculei.
7,9 $ Basidia with 6-8-sterigmata, spores usually smooth or slightly warted
8,0 $ Spores globose with regular profile, (5.5-)7-10.5 µm  in diam, ornamented with straight aculei, 1-3 µm  long $ B. isabellinum
8,0 $ Spores subglobose to ovoid or subpyriform , 7-13 x 6-12 µm , ornamented with slightly curved aculei, (2.5-)3-4 µm  $ B. bondarcevii
9,0 $ Spores globose to subglobose $ B. botryoideum
9,10 $ Spores differently shaped
10,11 $ Spores ellipsoid to ovoid
10,15 $ Spores navicularto subcylindrical 
11,12$ Spores smooth
11, 14$ Spores ornamented
12,0 $ At least the basal hyphae coarsely aspernlate $ B. pruinatum
12,13 $ AlI hyphae smooth or very scarcely ornamented
13,0 $ Spores 8-12 x 4--5.5(-6) µm , basal hyphae 8-13 µm  wide $ B. obtusisporum
13,0 $ Spores 5-8 x 2.5-4 µm , basal hyphae 10-20 µm  wide $ B. laeve
14,0 $ Spores ellipsoid to ovoid, slightly thick-walled, 5.2-6.7(-7) x 3.2-4.3 µm  $ B. stigmatisporum
14,0 $ Spores ellipsoid to subglobose, thick-walIed, 4.5-5.5 x 3.5-4.5 µm  $ B. asperulum
15,16 $ Spores broadly' navicular 10 broadly subcylindrical, L/W = 1.9-2.3
15,18 $ Spores narrowly subcylindrical to navicular, L/W 2.7-3.3
16,0 $ Basidia 15-25 µm  long, spores 8-12 x 4-6.5 µm . Anamorph unknown $ B. vagum
16,17 $ Basidia shorter, spores smaller. $ (4-species group, examination ofanamorph needed)
17,0 $ Basidia 13-20 x 7-10 µm , cylindrical 10 slightly constricted at maturity, 6-spored, spores  6-9 x 3-4 µm . Anamorph: Haplotrichum rubiginosum $ B. robustius *
17,0 $ Basidia 12-15(-18) x 5-8 µm , cylindrical, 6-spored, spores 6-8 x 3-4 µm , apically pointed. Anamorph: Haplotrichum capitatum $ B. candicans *
17,0 $ Basidia 12-18(-20) x 6-8 µm , cylindrical to slightly constricted at maturity, 6-spored, spores blunt, 6-9(-10) x 3-4.5 µm . Anamorph: Haplotrichum aureum $ B. aureum *
17,0 $ Basidia 12.5-19 x 7-9 µm , cylindrical, 4-- to 8-spored. Spores blunt, 8-9.5 x 3.5-4.5 µm . Anamorph: Haplotrichum ellipsosporum $ B. ellipsosporum *
18,0 $ Spores very long, 12-18.5 x 4--5 µm  $ B. danicum
18,19 $ Spores shorter
