titre$ Key to the anamorphs of the European species of Botryobasidium
1,0 $ Conidiophores with clamps, conidia 20-27 x 7-9(-10) µm . $Haplotrichum anamorph of B. ponderosum
1,2 $ Conidiophores without clamps
2,0 $ Conidiophores oftwo types: a) short, thin-walled, branched and more or less hyaline; b) long, thick-walled, unbranched and dark pigmented, conidia 17-25 x 14-22 µm  $ Haplotrichum simile
2,3 $ AlI conidiophores ofthe same type
3,0 $ Conidia fusiform, 15-25 x 6-8 µm  $ Haplotrichum medium
3,4 $ Conidia globo se to ellipsoid or lemon-shaped
4,5 $ Upper, conidiogenous part of the conidiophores unbranched, acropetal chains absent..
4,6 $ Conidiogenous part usually branched, acropetal chains present or absent..
5,0 $ Conidia (18-)20-25 x 10-13 µm , produced by a few conidiogenous teeth on the two distal cells ofthe conidiophore $ Haplotrichum ellipsosporum
5,0 $ Conidia, (13-)19-22 x 9-13 µm , produced by numerous conidiogenous teeth on the 3-4 distal celIs ofthe conidiophore $ Haplotrichum conspersum
6,7 $ Conidia globose to subglobose or broadly elIipsoid
6,9 $ Conidia ellipsoid or lemon-shaped
7,0 $ Conidiophores rarely anastomosing, conidia globo se, (8-)11-16 µm ; thin- to moderately thick-walled (up to 0.5 µm ), conidial surface slightly rough $ Haplotrichum curtisii
7,8 $ Conidiophores frequently anastomosing, conidial wall smooth, thicker (up to 1.5 µm )
8,0 $ Conidia born in acropeta1 chains, subg10bose to broad1y ellipsoid, 17-25 x 14-22 µm  $ Haplotrichum simile
8,0 $ Conidia born singly, not in acropetal chains, 13-17.5 x 13-15 µm , globose to broadly ellipsoid $ Haplotrichum rubiginosum
9,0 $ Conidia 13-16(-19) x 8-10 µm  $ Haplotrichum capitatum
9,0 $ Conidia 20-30 x 10-14.5 µm  $ Haplotrichum aureum

